WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:52.241
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:52.511 --> 00:53.345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

3
00:53.471 --> 00:54.305
ARE FICTITIOUS

4
00:54.430 --> 00:55.264
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

5
00:55.473 --> 00:56.348
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

6
01:08.360 --> 01:09.361
I…

7
01:10.237 --> 01:11.864
kissed this man.

8
01:41.727 --> 01:43.103
YEONG-DO

9
01:44.563 --> 01:45.397
What's up?

10
01:45.523 --> 01:46.982
Namgung!

11
01:47.107 --> 01:48.567
Come to the karaoke.

12
01:48.692 --> 01:50.152
Get over here right now!

13
01:50.277 --> 01:52.488
-What are you doing? -Let go of me!

14
01:52.613 --> 01:53.447
Punk!

15
01:54.365 --> 01:56.158
-What the heck? -I'm so sorry.

16
01:56.283 --> 01:57.117
I apologize.

17
01:59.370 --> 02:01.580
I'm going crazy. I can't stop him now.

18
02:01.705 --> 02:02.998
-Get here now! -Gosh.

19
02:05.459 --> 02:07.336
Hang on. I'll be right there.

20
02:17.596 --> 02:19.139
I don't know what you mean.

21
02:19.265 --> 02:21.058
Were you dreaming or something?

22
02:24.436 --> 02:25.771
You don't remember?

23
02:25.896 --> 02:28.691
I tend to black out when I drink.

24
02:30.526 --> 02:32.987
If I made a mistake, I apologize.

25
02:33.737 --> 02:36.782
It didn't mean anything, so don't worry…

26
02:53.591 --> 02:54.967
You really forgot?

27
02:58.929 --> 02:59.972
I don't think so.

28
03:00.556 --> 03:02.850
You look like you remember everything.

29
03:08.981 --> 03:10.733
"I'll let you quit directing."

30
03:13.402 --> 03:16.196
"I can do what your boyfriend

31
03:18.157 --> 03:19.575
can never do for you."

32
03:22.912 --> 03:24.204
Well?

33
03:26.916 --> 03:28.334
Is it coming back to you?

34
03:32.379 --> 03:33.923
I know you're confused.

35
03:34.632 --> 03:37.259
I came here because I'm just as confused.

36
03:39.261 --> 03:41.180
So I want to make a proposal.

37
03:43.265 --> 03:44.975
Let's have some fun for a bit.

38
03:46.143 --> 03:48.354
For you, a fling before marriage.

39
03:48.479 --> 03:50.606
And for me, just enough entertainment

40
03:52.399 --> 03:53.734
until I lose interest.

41
03:53.859 --> 03:55.945
We'll keep it at that.

42
03:57.821 --> 03:58.697
How about it?

43
04:01.408 --> 04:02.743
What do you think?

44
04:04.203 --> 04:05.746
-It wouldn't be too bad-- -You jerk!

45
04:05.871 --> 04:06.789
Hey!

46
04:16.507 --> 04:18.133
I regret what happened

47
04:18.258 --> 04:21.845
so much that I could die.

48
04:21.971 --> 04:23.097
So please,

49
04:23.722 --> 04:25.891
stay out of my sight.

50
04:26.433 --> 04:28.310
Please, please.

51
04:28.852 --> 04:30.104
I'm begging you.

52
04:30.688 --> 04:31.522
Please.

53
05:20.320 --> 05:21.321
HONDURAS KARAOKE

54
05:27.119 --> 05:28.162
The watch.

55
05:28.829 --> 05:31.331
That damn watch he wears every single day.

56
05:31.915 --> 05:33.542
All this fuss over that watch.

57
05:33.667 --> 05:35.294
He's completely lost it.

58
05:35.419 --> 05:37.838
He tore up the house, the salon, and now here.

59
05:38.505 --> 05:40.674
Good thing Mom is on a trip.

60
05:40.799 --> 05:42.718
Or she would've collapsed again.

61
05:51.643 --> 05:53.645
You were wearing it until yesterday.

62
05:55.856 --> 05:58.567
Yes, I was.

63
06:00.360 --> 06:01.987
I don't know. It just disappeared.

64
06:02.696 --> 06:04.907
It's not like Bo-ra bought it for you.

65
06:05.032 --> 06:07.868
You got it when you joined the Gyenam City team.

66
06:07.993 --> 06:09.244
Yeong-do.

67
06:10.704 --> 06:12.873
How long are you going to live like this?

68
06:12.998 --> 06:17.127
Do we have to keep walking on eggshells every time you flip out like this?

69
06:19.463 --> 06:20.923
Bo-ra's ashes are in it.

70
06:27.805 --> 06:29.139
Bo-ra's ashes

71
06:30.390 --> 06:32.267
are inside the watch.

72
06:52.913 --> 06:54.289
-Hey! -Huh?

73
06:58.669 --> 07:00.212
No, wait…

74
07:00.337 --> 07:01.421
-Follow me. -Wait.

75
07:01.547 --> 07:04.383
-Wait a minute! -Come here.

76
07:09.096 --> 07:10.139
Well…

77
07:11.598 --> 07:12.558
There's this

78
07:13.225 --> 07:15.310
challenge called "'99 Again"

79
07:16.895 --> 07:18.438
that's trending.

80
07:20.399 --> 07:22.317
So I borrowed Dad's suit,

81
07:23.569 --> 07:25.195
but it felt incomplete.

82
07:25.320 --> 07:27.739
Then I saw you sleeping,

83
07:28.949 --> 07:30.576
and I saw the watch.

84
07:31.410 --> 07:33.328
It looked so old and vintage,

85
07:35.164 --> 07:39.209
so I just wanted to wear it for a bit and then put it back.

86
07:42.921 --> 07:45.507
So where is it? Where's the watch now?

87
07:45.632 --> 07:48.635
Hey, yelling at him won't solve anything.

88
07:49.636 --> 07:52.222
Lee Sang-su, answer me straight.

89
07:54.349 --> 07:55.976
You lost the watch, didn't you?

90
07:59.396 --> 08:02.024
No, I mean…

91
08:02.858 --> 08:05.861
I had it on when I was filming,

92
08:08.530 --> 08:11.491
but then it suddenly disappeared. I was scared--

93
08:11.617 --> 08:12.659
Hey!

94
08:15.746 --> 08:17.164
Why are you yelling at me?

95
08:18.207 --> 08:20.584
Why are you crying? Stop crying!

96
08:22.377 --> 08:23.754
You, too. Calm down.

97
08:23.879 --> 08:26.006
He can't speak if you yell at him.

98
08:26.131 --> 08:27.883
Yeong-do, if I don't find that watch,

99
08:28.592 --> 08:29.968
I won't let this go.

100
08:31.386 --> 08:32.888
I'm done with you two.

101
08:33.013 --> 08:33.972
Hey.

102
08:34.097 --> 08:36.683
You're saying that to your brother over some watch?

103
08:39.436 --> 08:40.312
"Some watch"?

104
08:43.941 --> 08:45.275
Both of you, stop.

105
08:46.109 --> 08:48.237
Fighting like this won't solve anything.

106
08:49.321 --> 08:50.405
Sang-su, stop crying.

107
08:52.449 --> 08:53.951
It's getting late.

108
08:54.576 --> 08:56.536
Let's check the stream first thing tomorrow.

109
08:57.246 --> 09:00.290
Sang-su, send me all the footage.

110
09:00.415 --> 09:02.793
We need the exact spot to narrow the search.

111
09:14.596 --> 09:17.432
Stop crying. What are you even crying for?

112
09:18.225 --> 09:20.978
What if Aunt Bo-ra comes for me?

113
09:21.103 --> 09:22.646
I'm scared.

114
09:22.771 --> 09:24.189
That won't happen.

115
09:24.314 --> 09:26.942
He said Aunt Bo-ra's ashes were in the watch.

116
09:27.067 --> 09:28.443
I had no idea.

117
09:28.986 --> 09:31.154
I wore it and danced to "Boom Boom Boom."

118
09:31.280 --> 09:33.365
I even did Bollywood dances.

119
09:33.490 --> 09:34.658
That Bo-ra…

120
09:35.325 --> 09:37.619
She never visited Wan-do in four years.

121
09:38.287 --> 09:39.246
Don't worry.

122
09:39.830 --> 09:42.457
But since I lost the watch,

123
09:43.083 --> 09:44.501
she might come to punish me.

124
09:44.626 --> 09:47.087
Then tell her to go see your uncle.

125
09:56.013 --> 09:56.847
Actually, no.

126
09:59.349 --> 10:00.559
Sang-su.

127
10:01.643 --> 10:03.645
If Aunt Bo-ra pays you a visit,

128
10:04.354 --> 10:06.189
you have to beg her

129
10:06.857 --> 10:08.442
not to go see your uncle.

130
10:09.276 --> 10:10.110
What?

131
10:11.903 --> 10:13.030
No way.

132
10:13.822 --> 10:15.907
Why would you say that?

133
10:16.033 --> 10:17.409
I'm scared!

134
10:17.534 --> 10:19.536
Stop crying and tell her exactly this.

135
10:21.038 --> 10:23.457
Tell her to stay away from Wan-do.

136
10:23.582 --> 10:25.334
To please let him live in peace.

137
10:26.460 --> 10:28.503
To please just leave him alone.

138
10:29.171 --> 10:31.631
Why are you doing this? It's scary.

139
10:35.260 --> 10:36.720
Your mom's side is Catholic.

140
10:37.637 --> 10:39.931
We have six priests in the family.

141
10:41.141 --> 10:42.684
You'll be fine, Gabriel.

142
10:44.311 --> 10:46.396
Look, I'm sorry!

143
10:47.064 --> 10:48.607
Stop it!

144
10:48.732 --> 10:50.025
Come on, let's go.

145
10:52.527 --> 10:53.945
Gabriel…

146
11:18.929 --> 11:19.971
Mi-do, you asleep?

147
11:21.681 --> 11:23.725
You never go to sleep before 2 a.m.

148
11:27.521 --> 11:29.689
I'm completely done with that woman.

149
11:31.566 --> 11:33.693
I'll never see her again.

150
11:38.949 --> 11:40.075
Hey, are you crying?

151
11:45.038 --> 11:46.957
Why are you crying? You're making me sad.

152
11:51.545 --> 11:54.756
Namgung, what happened to your face?

153
11:54.881 --> 11:55.924
Did she do that?

154
12:01.304 --> 12:02.722
It's all over now.

155
12:04.850 --> 12:07.811
You won't have to worry about this ever again.

156
12:11.231 --> 12:12.607
So please stop crying.

157
12:15.819 --> 12:17.654
Don't cry.

158
12:29.249 --> 12:35.130
6. WHO IS OUR BEST HERO?

159
12:36.339 --> 12:37.674
Take a look at this.

160
12:39.009 --> 12:40.802
I trusted her to close up,

161
12:40.927 --> 12:44.389
but she was secretly taking customers late at night.

162
12:44.514 --> 12:46.057
Unbelievable.

163
12:56.776 --> 12:58.069
What are you doing?

164
12:58.195 --> 13:00.447
I was going to call the cops,

165
13:00.572 --> 13:03.241
but I called the family contact on your resume first.

166
13:03.366 --> 13:04.326
So ungrateful.

167
13:07.287 --> 13:08.246
What will you do?

168
13:09.039 --> 13:10.165
Are you going to pay

169
13:11.541 --> 13:12.751
3.2 million won?

170
13:13.835 --> 13:14.878
She's not family.

171
13:16.630 --> 13:17.672
She's a friend.

172
13:17.797 --> 13:19.090
Talk to me.

173
13:21.843 --> 13:22.844
Call the cops.

174
13:27.140 --> 13:28.725
That'll teach her a lesson.

175
13:39.027 --> 13:40.362
ATM

176
13:40.487 --> 13:43.949
Please take your card. Cash will be dispensed.

177
13:44.074 --> 13:45.492
Please take your cash.

178
13:45.617 --> 13:47.244
CASH DISPENSER

179
13:49.204 --> 13:51.331
Thank you for your transaction. Have a nice day.

180
13:55.377 --> 13:56.211
Su-a.

181
14:00.298 --> 14:01.967
The salon owner does this a lot.

182
14:02.801 --> 14:04.844
We fought over my days off.

183
14:04.970 --> 14:07.055
She promised to help with my training,

184
14:07.180 --> 14:08.848
then she treated me like a thief.

185
14:12.602 --> 14:13.436
You…

186
14:17.357 --> 14:18.858
don't believe me, do you?

187
14:19.568 --> 14:20.652
Then earn my trust.

188
14:22.028 --> 14:23.154
With the CCTV footage,

189
14:23.280 --> 14:25.615
your online post, the contract,

190
14:25.740 --> 14:28.243
and how you ignored the owner's calls,

191
14:29.202 --> 14:30.829
how can I trust you?

192
14:46.845 --> 14:47.679
HYDROCOLLOID BANDAGE

193
14:49.848 --> 14:51.933
Don't use the bandage on your face.

194
14:52.934 --> 14:54.686
It'll scar your pretty face.

195
14:55.979 --> 14:59.816
I'll get my things tomorrow when you go to work.

196
14:59.941 --> 15:01.651
I'll pay you back soon, too.

197
15:06.740 --> 15:08.241
Sorry for bothering you.

198
15:09.618 --> 15:10.577
I won't ever…

199
15:11.870 --> 15:13.121
contact you again.

200
15:47.238 --> 15:50.992
Make sure you eat. Eat everything even if you're not hungry.

201
15:51.117 --> 15:52.452
And take your red ginseng.

202
16:10.345 --> 16:12.347
Mi-do has been acting weird.

203
16:14.808 --> 16:15.684
Why?

204
16:15.809 --> 16:17.102
Because you met your mom?

205
16:17.227 --> 16:19.938
Still? That was days ago.

206
16:20.605 --> 16:22.065
Yes, but…

207
16:30.240 --> 16:31.074
What's wrong?

208
16:32.325 --> 16:33.827
Why are you crying?

209
16:33.952 --> 16:35.203
Looks good.

210
16:40.458 --> 16:41.876
What's wrong, Mi-do?

211
16:45.755 --> 16:47.173
Why do you keep crying?

212
17:02.939 --> 17:05.442
Mi-do cries whenever she sees me these days.

213
17:05.567 --> 17:06.526
She just

214
17:07.360 --> 17:09.487
keeps crying.

215
17:09.612 --> 17:11.114
Is she going through menopause?

216
17:12.157 --> 17:14.117
Lots of women get it in their thirties.

217
17:14.242 --> 17:15.118
Come on.

218
17:16.202 --> 17:17.412
Don't be ridiculous.

219
17:17.537 --> 17:18.955
How else can you explain it?

220
17:19.664 --> 17:22.333
Why would a tough girl like her cry every day?

221
17:23.001 --> 17:25.670
You were crying every day too after the divorce. Remember?

222
17:25.795 --> 17:27.964
Why would you bring that up now?

223
17:29.215 --> 17:30.383
What about you?

224
17:31.259 --> 17:32.385
Sulking because of your nephew.

225
17:33.595 --> 17:35.597
I heard you ignored Sang-su's text last night.

226
17:35.722 --> 17:37.390
That kid…

227
17:37.515 --> 17:39.058
Tell him to stay away.

228
17:39.809 --> 17:41.811
Hey, man, he's 14 years old.

229
17:41.936 --> 17:44.105
Aren't embarrassed to be fighting with a kid?

230
17:44.230 --> 17:45.148
What about you?

231
17:45.774 --> 17:47.984
You fight with that kid. Aren't you embarrassed?

232
17:48.109 --> 17:50.111
Oh, you little punk.

233
17:57.535 --> 17:58.411
Keep going.

234
17:58.536 --> 18:00.789
Why don't you keep going?

235
18:00.914 --> 18:02.415
Why don't you do it right?

236
18:02.540 --> 18:04.000
Don't half-ass it.

237
18:04.667 --> 18:07.504
Should I call Ms. Ma, Mi-do, and Sang-su, all of them?

238
18:10.089 --> 18:11.466
Jeez, seriously.

239
18:11.591 --> 18:12.884
You guys fight every day.

240
18:21.601 --> 18:23.144
-Where is it? -Namgung.

241
18:24.979 --> 18:25.814
Are you…

242
18:27.065 --> 18:27.982
okay?

243
18:28.107 --> 18:30.026
What? I can't hear you.

244
18:30.777 --> 18:31.736
I mean…

245
18:34.405 --> 18:36.241
you met with your mom.

246
18:41.287 --> 18:42.580
Right. Ho.

247
18:43.164 --> 18:43.998
Are you okay?

248
18:44.123 --> 18:46.125
I heard she caused trouble again.

249
18:47.085 --> 18:47.961
Nothing serious, right?

250
18:48.086 --> 18:49.254
Of course it's serious.

251
18:51.589 --> 18:54.384
A warrant was issued, and she's in a detention center.

252
18:54.926 --> 18:55.844
Hey!

253
18:57.762 --> 18:59.848
-You scared me. -If that happened,

254
18:59.973 --> 19:01.474
you should've told us right away.

255
19:01.599 --> 19:03.268
You just said you saw her,

256
19:03.393 --> 19:05.645
so I thought it was just about money again.

257
19:06.980 --> 19:08.523
Why are you always like this?

258
19:08.648 --> 19:09.816
Does Mi-do know?

259
19:09.941 --> 19:12.110
She's been acting weird because of you.

260
19:12.235 --> 19:13.820
Why are you like this?

261
19:13.945 --> 19:15.655
Always telling us when it's over.

262
19:15.780 --> 19:17.907
Didn't I tell you never to do that again?

263
19:18.032 --> 19:19.742
Stop doing that.

264
19:19.868 --> 19:21.744
We're friends. It really hurts.

265
19:24.038 --> 19:26.040
I'd feel so pathetic telling you.

266
19:31.713 --> 19:34.048
The fact that a woman like her is my mom

267
19:36.050 --> 19:38.261
is just so pathetic and embarrassing.

268
19:41.723 --> 19:43.141
I feel so pathetic and embarrassed

269
19:45.226 --> 19:47.186
in front of you and Wan-do,

270
19:48.313 --> 19:49.939
and especially in front of Mi-do.

271
19:52.400 --> 19:53.818
So I couldn't tell you.

272
19:55.028 --> 19:55.945
I'm sorry.

273
19:58.740 --> 19:59.741
Oh, jeez.

274
20:02.076 --> 20:02.911
Goodness.

275
20:05.747 --> 20:07.373
Say that one more time.

276
20:07.498 --> 20:08.750
I'll seriously get mad.

277
20:08.875 --> 20:11.961
Yes, I'll get mad, too!

278
20:13.463 --> 20:15.632
I was too embarrassed to tell you this,

279
20:16.299 --> 20:18.635
but in the last civil service exam I failed,

280
20:18.760 --> 20:21.429
my average wasn't 55. It was 37.

281
20:22.263 --> 20:26.309
Yes, and I was too embarrassed to say this too,

282
20:26.434 --> 20:28.061
but my driving test…

283
20:28.686 --> 20:32.607
I didn't fail four times. I failed seven times.

284
20:38.279 --> 20:42.325
You took the civil service exam for three straight years and got a 37?

285
20:43.868 --> 20:45.536
Are you even an athlete?

286
20:45.662 --> 20:48.665
How do you fail a driving test seven times?

287
20:52.126 --> 20:54.337
That's hilarious, man.

288
20:54.462 --> 20:55.588
Hey, get that punk.

289
20:55.713 --> 20:57.715
-Hey! -Get him!

290
20:57.840 --> 20:59.258
No!

291
20:59.384 --> 21:01.302
-Get him! -Wait!

292
21:02.762 --> 21:04.764
Time out!

293
21:04.889 --> 21:05.807
Ouch!

294
21:07.642 --> 21:09.394
Hey, the watch!

295
21:09.519 --> 21:11.229
I won't fall for that twice, punk!

296
21:11.354 --> 21:14.273
No, I'm serious! Look!

297
21:39.674 --> 21:41.342
How many meters today?

298
21:45.013 --> 21:46.305
210 meters.

299
21:49.225 --> 21:51.144
Still so deep.

300
22:03.072 --> 22:05.116
When we scattered Bo-ra into the sea…

301
22:10.288 --> 22:12.623
something got caught in my hand.

302
22:16.669 --> 22:17.837
THE LATE BAEK BO-RA

303
22:18.880 --> 22:20.465
Bo-ra…

304
22:23.468 --> 22:27.305
No, Bo-ra!

305
23:16.145 --> 23:17.605
I'm really pathetic, aren't I?

306
23:51.180 --> 23:52.348
I regret what happened

307
23:53.182 --> 23:56.519
so much that I could die.

308
23:57.186 --> 23:59.397
Stay out of my sight.

309
24:04.443 --> 24:05.695
Damn it.

310
24:18.541 --> 24:20.835
Let's discuss the case about the researcher in person.

311
24:20.960 --> 24:22.336
Not over the phone.

312
24:22.461 --> 24:24.255
The researcher isn't the issue.

313
24:24.380 --> 24:25.798
Didn't you hear about Jisang?

314
24:26.382 --> 24:28.634
Things are looking bad at Jisang.

315
24:29.260 --> 24:30.845
I think something went wrong.

316
24:30.970 --> 24:33.890
Last night, the cops and the Financial Supervisory Service

317
24:34.015 --> 24:37.727
raided Line's accounting HQ and seized all their servers.

318
24:37.852 --> 24:39.812
Didn't Mr. Seo tell you anything?

319
24:40.855 --> 24:41.689
Hello?

320
24:42.607 --> 24:44.108
Are you listening?

321
24:44.942 --> 24:46.652
Gosh, is he listening or not?

322
24:53.826 --> 24:56.579
Mr. Han, why don't you take a vacation?

323
24:58.122 --> 24:59.040
You know…

324
25:00.124 --> 25:02.793
you haven't had a break since the Cheonsong Electronics case.

325
25:02.919 --> 25:05.171
Let Attorney Lee finish up Jisang's case.

326
25:05.296 --> 25:07.423
Get some fresh air for two weeks.

327
25:07.548 --> 25:09.342
We still have the appeal.

328
25:11.093 --> 25:12.553
I have to settle this.

329
25:14.222 --> 25:15.514
Jisang's cash flow

330
25:16.724 --> 25:19.894
will be cut off once the damages claim is enforced.

331
25:20.019 --> 25:21.229
Mediation is the only option.

332
25:22.313 --> 25:24.482
Chairman Ko will accept it soon.

333
25:28.110 --> 25:30.988
I didn't expect to be sent off empty-handed like this.

334
25:36.327 --> 25:37.161
What was that?

335
25:41.916 --> 25:43.584
You have no conscience.

336
25:44.377 --> 25:46.003
You worked me to the bone.

337
25:48.965 --> 25:51.842
You should at least get me a business-class ticket.

338
25:55.638 --> 25:57.181
I'll get you first class.

339
25:57.974 --> 26:00.142
Just say the word. Where to?

340
26:04.063 --> 26:05.773
I don't want anywhere too hot.

341
26:08.234 --> 26:09.819
Or too humid.

342
26:24.250 --> 26:25.334
So I'm a dog?

343
26:25.459 --> 26:27.128
A lapdog, to be exact.

344
26:27.253 --> 26:30.047
A lapdog who could get dumped by his master any second.

345
26:30.965 --> 26:32.008
Hi.

346
26:36.304 --> 26:39.849
This is a piece called a knight in a game called chess.

347
26:40.641 --> 26:43.269
It's the most unpredictable piece in chess.

348
26:44.186 --> 26:45.021
The knight.

349
26:46.564 --> 26:49.025
A rook can only move in straight lines,

350
26:49.150 --> 26:50.401
but not this one.

351
26:52.403 --> 26:54.864
Even when it seems completely blocked,

352
26:56.741 --> 26:58.492
it moves in an L-shape

353
26:59.702 --> 27:00.745
to create a chance.

354
27:01.537 --> 27:04.707
It may look like a dead end, but it's not over.

355
27:04.832 --> 27:07.001
Even if it doesn't go straight,

356
27:07.960 --> 27:11.839
it can freely change the game as it moves on the board.

357
27:12.882 --> 27:13.716
I'm here…

358
27:15.426 --> 27:16.761
to give you

359
27:17.553 --> 27:19.180
that chance right now.

360
27:21.057 --> 27:23.559
Whether you tell me the truth or not,

361
27:24.352 --> 27:26.270
I plan to make it happen.

362
27:27.772 --> 27:30.358
So trust me now,

363
27:32.401 --> 27:34.570
and tell me what happened to you that night.

364
27:35.905 --> 27:37.031
Will you?

365
28:08.813 --> 28:10.189
Mi-do, are you up?

366
28:10.815 --> 28:11.690
Still not feeling well?

367
28:11.816 --> 28:12.650
MIDORI

368
28:12.775 --> 28:14.735
Want to get chicken feet from Bongcheon later?

369
28:19.198 --> 28:20.491
46TH COHORT LEE MIN-GI: DID YOU SEE THE JOB POST FOR THE POSITION IN FRANCE?

370
28:24.036 --> 28:26.330
Did you see the job post for the position in France?

371
28:34.171 --> 28:37.341
What are you looking at so intently, Mr. Namgung?

372
28:38.384 --> 28:40.177
EXPAT POSITION IN PARIS CONFECTIONERY MARKETING & SALES

373
28:40.302 --> 28:41.762
Are you applying for it?

374
28:42.805 --> 28:45.266
I'm thinking about it. The perks are pretty good.

375
28:45.391 --> 28:46.559
Wow, you traitor.

376
28:46.684 --> 28:48.352
What about our Spicy SweeTato Chips?

377
28:49.270 --> 28:52.356
I was going to bail if it didn't launch by Q3 next year anyway.

378
28:52.481 --> 28:54.608
You're so bold when the boss is away.

379
28:54.733 --> 28:56.026
I'm telling on you.

380
28:57.069 --> 28:59.405
You probably wouldn't get it anyway.

381
29:00.573 --> 29:03.075
I heard about this from a friend in HR.

382
29:03.200 --> 29:04.702
They need a French speaker.

383
29:04.827 --> 29:06.245
I double-majored in French.

384
29:06.370 --> 29:07.246
What?

385
29:07.371 --> 29:08.747
My GPA was 4.3.

386
29:09.457 --> 29:11.625
I wiped the floor with the French majors.

387
29:12.460 --> 29:13.627
What?

388
29:13.752 --> 29:16.464
Why are you so fluent? Why is your accent so good?

389
29:16.589 --> 29:19.008
-Are you-- -Are you really going?

390
29:19.133 --> 29:21.135
Why?

391
29:22.261 --> 29:23.637
Launching isn't the end.

392
29:23.762 --> 29:25.306
What about marketing? Pop-ups?

393
29:26.515 --> 29:30.144
Wow, were you always this irresponsible?

394
29:30.269 --> 29:31.937
Or is it because of ambition?

395
29:32.062 --> 29:35.232
Because expats are first in line for promotions?

396
29:35.900 --> 29:37.818
Or is it the salary?

397
29:37.943 --> 29:40.613
If not that, is it the MBA tuition support?

398
29:40.738 --> 29:42.281
Is it because of that?

399
29:45.659 --> 29:47.369
It's on my girlfriend's bucket list.

400
29:53.042 --> 29:56.795
My girlfriend has always wanted to live in Paris.

401
29:57.630 --> 29:58.964
She's been down lately.

402
29:59.089 --> 30:01.592
Two years there would be a nice change of pace.

403
30:02.760 --> 30:04.053
Will the competition be tough?

404
30:06.013 --> 30:07.264
Mr. Namgung.

405
30:08.182 --> 30:09.725
Are you getting married?

406
30:10.392 --> 30:12.061
You are, right?

407
30:12.895 --> 30:14.813
Wow, congratulations!

408
30:15.481 --> 30:16.607
Pretend you don't know.

409
30:16.732 --> 30:19.443
If the boss knows I didn't tell him, he'll pout for a week.

410
30:19.568 --> 30:23.072
You're finally off the market.

411
30:23.197 --> 30:25.032
Seriously, congratulations.

412
30:25.991 --> 30:28.661
Isn't your girlfriend your first love?

413
30:31.830 --> 30:33.832
You don't have an appointment.

414
30:34.917 --> 30:38.337
I'm asking because he won't answer!

415
30:38.462 --> 30:41.382
Assistant Manager Namgung Ho with TF Snack Team 3!

416
30:41.507 --> 30:44.677
If you keep making a scene, we'll have to call the police.

417
30:44.802 --> 30:46.345
Want to see a real scene?

418
30:46.470 --> 30:48.389
Just make one phone call!

419
30:48.514 --> 30:49.682
-You need to leave. -What?

420
30:49.807 --> 30:51.058
-I warned you. -Leave?

421
30:51.183 --> 30:52.226
-Leave where? -Why?

422
30:52.351 --> 30:54.353
-Call the cops! -Okay.

423
30:54.478 --> 30:56.480
-Get out. -You want to do this?

424
30:56.605 --> 30:57.565
-Hit me. -You punk!

425
31:03.737 --> 31:05.322
Well, look who it is.

426
31:05.447 --> 31:07.157
Our precious debtor.

427
31:08.534 --> 31:10.536
You're much more handsome in person.

428
31:11.704 --> 31:12.788
Nice to meet you.

429
31:16.208 --> 31:18.002
Let's take this outside.

430
31:24.091 --> 31:26.760
Namgung, I'm at a cafe near your office.

431
31:26.885 --> 31:29.013
I'll write here until you're off work.

432
31:29.138 --> 31:30.097
Let's get dinner.

433
31:30.222 --> 31:32.683
Did Mr. Namgung take out a private loan?

434
31:33.350 --> 31:35.185
No way.

435
31:35.311 --> 31:38.480
I worked with him at the pop-up. He's definitely not like that.

436
31:38.606 --> 31:41.066
Then why would a loan shark come here?

437
31:41.191 --> 31:42.401
We all saw it.

438
31:42.526 --> 31:44.153
He must have his reasons.

439
31:44.278 --> 31:47.072
Come to think of it, when Assistant Manager Gung was new,

440
31:47.197 --> 31:49.116
I heard something similar happened.

441
31:49.241 --> 31:50.117
What?

442
31:50.242 --> 31:53.203
He was the first rookie to get his paycheck garnished.

443
31:53.329 --> 31:55.331
There was a lot of talk in the finance team.

444
31:56.832 --> 31:58.000
I think I heard about that too.

445
31:58.125 --> 31:59.793
Was he gambling?

446
31:59.918 --> 32:02.254
Like sports betting or something?

447
32:03.130 --> 32:07.676
You know, those clean-cut guys usually have dirty secrets.

448
32:07.801 --> 32:09.011
Knock it off.

449
32:09.595 --> 32:12.306
Don't gossip when you don't know anything.

450
32:12.973 --> 32:14.683
I'm embarrassed to be your coworker.

451
32:14.808 --> 32:17.311
Focus on your own work instead of gossiping.

452
32:22.483 --> 32:24.693
-That scared me. -Seriously.

453
32:27.196 --> 32:28.322
Excuse me.

454
32:34.411 --> 32:36.872
The person you are calling is unavailable. Please leave a message…

455
32:37.414 --> 32:39.291
At what time did he leave with those guys?

456
32:39.416 --> 32:42.044
Less than 20 minutes ago. I'm sure he's fine.

457
32:44.254 --> 32:46.548
If it was serious, we'd have called 911.

458
32:46.674 --> 32:48.008
He said not to worry.

459
32:48.133 --> 32:49.927
You still should've called 911.

460
32:50.052 --> 32:51.762
Anything could happen.

461
32:52.763 --> 32:54.640
You're worrying too much.

462
32:54.765 --> 32:56.975
In broad daylight in Seoul? What could…

463
32:57.101 --> 32:58.894
But what if something does happen?

464
32:59.645 --> 33:02.272
What if something happens to Namgung?

465
33:06.694 --> 33:08.404
Oh, I'm sorry.

466
33:09.029 --> 33:11.949
I shouldn't take it out on you. I'm just so worried.

467
33:12.074 --> 33:13.575
I'm sorry. I really am.

468
33:28.465 --> 33:29.591
PROMISSORY NOTE STANDARD LOAN AGREEMENT

469
33:29.717 --> 33:30.551
Your mother,

470
33:30.676 --> 33:32.636
Choi Hwa-young, borrowed 300 million won.

471
33:32.761 --> 33:34.722
You know she's in custody, right?

472
33:34.847 --> 33:37.141
She'll be short on the interest payment starting this month,

473
33:37.266 --> 33:38.809
so we came a bit early.

474
33:39.476 --> 33:42.521
If you lent money to a con artist without collateral,

475
33:43.772 --> 33:46.316
wasn't that a risk you were willing to take?

476
33:48.485 --> 33:50.946
Who knew she'd blow it before she even started?

477
33:51.780 --> 33:54.116
I hear you're the one who messed it up.

478
33:54.241 --> 33:56.034
Then you should take the fall.

479
33:56.160 --> 33:59.747
By the way, you know renouncing your inheritance won't work, right?

480
33:59.872 --> 34:01.832
We don't care about the law--

481
34:03.167 --> 34:05.586
Seeing a guy like you reminds me of someone.

482
34:06.628 --> 34:08.464
This is the tibialis posterior.

483
34:09.339 --> 34:10.507
-What? -My biological father

484
34:10.632 --> 34:13.051
was supposedly great at cutting it.

485
34:13.802 --> 34:17.222
Guess he was a famous knifeman in your line of work.

486
34:19.057 --> 34:21.727
He crippled a ton of people.

487
34:22.811 --> 34:23.937
Choi Hwa-young said

488
34:24.062 --> 34:27.816
it was creepy how he'd giggle while he worked.

489
34:30.986 --> 34:32.321
Are you threatening me?

490
34:32.446 --> 34:33.947
It's not a threat.

491
34:34.072 --> 34:37.075
I'm just saying my blood is trash.

492
34:37.201 --> 34:40.204
Look, you think words like that would make us flinch?

493
34:40.871 --> 34:43.123
-We've seen tons of guys-- -I'm sure you have.

494
34:45.250 --> 34:46.835
But I'm different.

495
34:49.838 --> 34:50.964
I'm very different.

496
34:53.217 --> 34:54.343
You probably know,

497
34:54.468 --> 34:56.637
but I only have one kidney.

498
34:57.221 --> 34:59.431
I'm not giving up my liver or eyes.

499
35:00.557 --> 35:03.060
And you'd better not mess with the people around me.

500
35:05.604 --> 35:07.022
Who do you think you are?

501
35:08.148 --> 35:09.441
Why so confident?

502
35:10.234 --> 35:12.402
You have no idea what we can do.

503
35:12.528 --> 35:13.529
Sorry, but…

504
35:14.863 --> 35:16.949
I already died when I was seven,

505
35:19.952 --> 35:21.703
so I'm living on borrowed time.

506
35:25.707 --> 35:26.667
That's why…

507
35:30.087 --> 35:31.797
I'm not afraid of dying.

508
35:33.674 --> 35:35.092
Mess with me and see.

509
35:36.260 --> 35:38.220
I'll show you how crazy I can get.

510
35:47.396 --> 35:48.939
Excuse me!

511
35:53.360 --> 35:55.654
Seriously, congratulations.

512
35:55.779 --> 35:58.365
Isn't your girlfriend your first love?

513
36:00.033 --> 36:01.743
"First love…"

514
36:03.412 --> 36:05.205
is a bit too cheesy.

515
36:06.415 --> 36:08.500
If I had to describe her,

516
36:09.668 --> 36:10.878
maybe a hero?

517
36:12.963 --> 36:15.841
My girlfriend is really awesome.

518
36:17.426 --> 36:19.136
It's impossible

519
36:20.178 --> 36:21.847
for you not to…

520
36:26.310 --> 36:27.561
fall so hard for her.

521
36:32.024 --> 36:35.235
Lee Mi-do was the greatest hero in my life.

522
36:43.994 --> 36:48.123
After I died at seven, she revived me and then kept on saving me over and over.

523
36:48.248 --> 36:50.959
She's truly the greatest hero in my life.

524
36:51.627 --> 36:52.502
Die, you little shit!

525
36:53.837 --> 36:56.006
Damn you! My gosh.

526
36:57.925 --> 37:00.135
You little piece of shit.

527
37:06.350 --> 37:08.477
Namgung, are you okay?

528
37:09.144 --> 37:10.354
Namgung. Oh no.

529
37:11.855 --> 37:12.981
Are you all right?

530
37:19.446 --> 37:20.364
Mi-do.

531
37:24.409 --> 37:27.329
But since he's a minor, he'll be released soon, right?

532
37:29.164 --> 37:30.832
Everything he said is a lie.

533
37:39.341 --> 37:40.842
Namgung Ho was taking his midterms

534
37:40.968 --> 37:43.053
during the time the victim was texting them.

535
37:43.178 --> 37:46.014
The account is in Namgung Ho's name, but Aunt Hwa-young used it.

536
37:47.140 --> 37:49.726
The evidence is all here. Please check it.

537
37:50.560 --> 37:51.478
Damn it.

538
37:53.063 --> 37:55.107
What are you smiling at?

539
37:55.232 --> 37:56.858
You almost went to juvie.

540
37:58.944 --> 37:59.945
Ho!

541
38:03.699 --> 38:04.783
Ho!

542
38:06.118 --> 38:06.994
Ho!

543
38:07.119 --> 38:09.121
If you don't pay interest this month,

544
38:09.246 --> 38:11.164
you'll never see your son again.

545
38:12.958 --> 38:14.376
Then lend me another million won.

546
38:14.501 --> 38:15.460
What?

547
38:15.585 --> 38:18.588
You're taking my son as collateral anyway.

548
38:18.714 --> 38:20.841
Lend me one million… No, two million.

549
38:24.970 --> 38:28.306
Ho, Mom will come get you, okay?

550
38:30.726 --> 38:31.893
Lend it to me.

551
38:39.693 --> 38:41.486
I feel bad for you.

552
38:41.611 --> 38:43.447
For having a mom like that.

553
38:49.327 --> 38:50.245
A kid jumped out.

554
38:50.996 --> 38:53.123
-Are you okay? -What the…

555
38:54.958 --> 38:57.210
This is so freaking annoying.

556
38:58.253 --> 38:59.171
Hey!

557
39:30.827 --> 39:32.871
You know Granny Yong-seon from Busan, right?

558
39:34.414 --> 39:37.084
How do you know Ms. Yong-seon…

559
39:38.418 --> 39:39.961
MS. YONG-SEON FROM BUSAN

560
39:47.302 --> 39:48.303
Yes, ma'am.

561
39:49.346 --> 39:50.639
Yes.

562
39:51.389 --> 39:52.682
Sorry?

563
39:52.808 --> 39:54.017
Understood.

564
39:54.142 --> 39:55.852
I'll call you back.

565
39:59.272 --> 40:00.690
We'll pay off the debt.

566
40:01.483 --> 40:03.026
We'll pay monthly interest, too.

567
40:03.151 --> 40:03.985
But…

568
40:04.945 --> 40:08.031
we'll only pay the legal interest rate along with the principal.

569
40:08.156 --> 40:09.366
Mi-do, get up.

570
40:11.243 --> 40:12.911
Stay out of this. Get up.

571
40:15.705 --> 40:18.750
So don't ever show up at his work like this again.

572
40:19.584 --> 40:23.755
If… you come here and lay a finger on him,

573
40:24.881 --> 40:26.133
you're dead.

574
40:27.259 --> 40:29.469
I'll really kill you.

575
40:42.357 --> 40:43.316
Mi-do.

576
40:46.862 --> 40:47.946
Mi-do.

577
40:54.661 --> 40:55.912
I guess I anticipated this

578
40:56.037 --> 40:57.914
when I wrote a script involving loan sharks.

579
41:00.542 --> 41:02.919
Wow, I had such great foresight.

580
41:04.671 --> 41:06.798
Even though the movie fell through,

581
41:06.923 --> 41:10.594
sending Granny Yong-seon red ginseng every holiday paid off.

582
41:12.470 --> 41:13.597
Namgung.

583
41:14.931 --> 41:17.184
I'll work hard on my writing.

584
41:18.185 --> 41:21.146
I'll swallow my pride and debut.

585
41:21.855 --> 41:23.899
We can pay it off together, okay?

586
41:24.900 --> 41:27.152
Don't you dare get any crazy ideas.

587
41:27.819 --> 41:30.155
Don't even think about selling your liver or something.

588
41:34.743 --> 41:36.786
I know why you delayed our marriage.

589
41:39.122 --> 41:40.957
You said we'd wait until I debuted.

590
41:41.082 --> 41:42.959
That was just an excuse.

591
41:44.252 --> 41:45.795
It was because of your mom.

592
41:47.130 --> 41:48.590
You thought you'd burden me.

593
41:50.008 --> 41:52.761
I actually knew everything. I just pretended not to.

594
41:54.930 --> 41:56.306
Honestly,

595
41:57.515 --> 41:59.434
I was a little scared.

596
42:01.353 --> 42:02.812
But not anymore.

597
42:03.647 --> 42:06.399
I'm really not scared anymore.

598
42:09.361 --> 42:10.779
Don't say you're sorry.

599
42:11.446 --> 42:13.031
Don't say thank you, either.

600
42:13.949 --> 42:14.950
Just…

601
42:16.743 --> 42:17.911
don't say anything.

602
42:19.454 --> 42:20.705
Don't say anything.

603
42:50.193 --> 42:51.528
Let's go on a trip.

604
42:52.862 --> 42:54.072
A trip?

605
42:55.240 --> 42:56.074
Yes.

606
42:57.200 --> 42:58.410
Let's go to Taipei.

607
42:59.452 --> 43:00.870
It was great three years ago.

608
43:04.374 --> 43:07.043
Let's do all the sightseeing we missed last time.

609
43:08.086 --> 43:08.962
Like…

610
43:09.754 --> 43:11.381
the Shilin Night Market.

611
43:13.842 --> 43:17.637
And the place from Spirited Away. What was it called?

612
43:17.762 --> 43:20.181
-Jiufen? -Yes, let's go there, too.

613
43:21.266 --> 43:22.934
Can you get time off?

614
43:23.059 --> 43:24.269
You're busy at work.

615
43:26.062 --> 43:27.522
I'll make it happen.

616
43:30.191 --> 43:31.318
Let's go.

617
43:32.527 --> 43:34.154
Really.

618
44:00.513 --> 44:01.556
Hello?

619
44:01.681 --> 44:03.892
What? She answers this number?

620
44:05.477 --> 44:07.187
Wow, that hurts my pride.

621
44:10.273 --> 44:11.858
This is so annoying.

622
44:12.776 --> 44:13.902
Gosh…

623
44:14.027 --> 44:16.321
Come on, give it to me.

624
44:16.446 --> 44:17.530
Hello?

625
44:17.655 --> 44:19.532
Do you live at Hines Officetel?

626
44:19.657 --> 44:21.910
I think you need to come outside.

627
44:22.035 --> 44:22.869
Excuse me?

628
44:22.994 --> 44:24.954
I'm in front of Hines Officetel,

629
44:25.080 --> 44:26.289
and my passenger is drunk.

630
44:27.791 --> 44:28.875
Hello, I--

631
44:42.889 --> 44:45.266
-Are you the one who answered the call? -I am.

632
44:45.392 --> 44:48.353
Why did it take you so long? I called so many times.

633
44:49.062 --> 44:52.315
He must've lost his wallet. He hasn't paid me yet.

634
44:53.525 --> 44:57.195
I'm sorry, but could you take him back to where he was?

635
44:57.320 --> 44:58.696
I'll pay for a round trip.

636
44:58.822 --> 44:59.906
That's a problem.

637
45:00.031 --> 45:01.950
I accepted a call when we spoke.

638
45:02.075 --> 45:04.202
If I cancel it now, I'll get a penalty.

639
45:07.122 --> 45:09.749
You can wire it to my account. It's 35,000 won.

640
45:09.874 --> 45:12.252
Oh, okay. Just a second.

641
45:17.090 --> 45:18.299
I sent it.

642
45:18.425 --> 45:19.467
Lee Mi-do, right?

643
45:19.592 --> 45:20.552
-Yes. -It went through.

644
45:20.677 --> 45:21.886
-Take care. -You too.

645
46:00.175 --> 46:02.218
Just so you don't get the wrong idea,

646
46:02.927 --> 46:06.556
I'm only doing this because I hate you being in my space.

647
46:09.350 --> 46:11.561
What the hell am I doing at this hour?

648
46:34.959 --> 46:36.002
Jeez.

649
47:02.779 --> 47:03.738
What?

650
47:04.864 --> 47:06.574
It really is Lee Mi-do.

651
47:07.742 --> 47:11.246
Mr. Han, you're very drunk. We can talk later.

652
47:15.083 --> 47:16.417
Later when?

653
47:17.126 --> 47:18.920
You blocked my number.

654
47:22.131 --> 47:24.259
I have a lot of pride, you know?

655
47:25.218 --> 47:27.762
I'd never call you

656
47:28.763 --> 47:30.598
using someone else's phone.

657
47:31.849 --> 47:34.519
That's the best thing I've heard from you.

658
47:35.562 --> 47:38.189
Make sure you keep that promise.

659
47:43.945 --> 47:46.030
This is annoying.

660
47:47.198 --> 47:49.075
You're not my type.

661
47:52.579 --> 47:54.956
I don't even like older women.

662
48:02.964 --> 48:03.881
What?

663
48:06.175 --> 48:07.051
I'm telling you,

664
48:08.052 --> 48:10.054
you're not my type.

665
48:17.604 --> 48:18.479
Okay.

666
48:20.023 --> 48:21.232
I admit you're cute.

667
48:22.734 --> 48:23.735
No, no.

668
48:26.237 --> 48:29.157
I admit you're really cute.

669
48:33.369 --> 48:34.829
No.

670
48:36.914 --> 48:38.791
You're not cute at all.

671
48:41.878 --> 48:43.171
This is so annoying.

672
48:53.264 --> 48:54.223
Don't laugh at me.

673
48:58.227 --> 48:59.771
No, do it again.

674
49:09.447 --> 49:10.531
Mr. Han.

675
49:11.699 --> 49:12.659
It's just that

676
49:13.284 --> 49:16.037
you've never met a crazy bitch like me,

677
49:16.954 --> 49:18.748
so you're just confused.

678
49:19.749 --> 49:21.459
In a few days,

679
49:21.584 --> 49:26.297
you'll just think, "Oh, there was that crazy bitch,"

680
49:27.590 --> 49:29.467
and you'll forget my face.

681
49:30.385 --> 49:31.427
So,

682
49:33.137 --> 49:34.847
just pretend you had cheap booze

683
49:36.265 --> 49:38.810
and got a bad stomachache,

684
49:42.188 --> 49:43.314
and forget about it.

685
49:47.110 --> 49:48.736
Want me to tell you a secret?

686
49:52.407 --> 49:53.950
I'm getting dumped soon.

687
50:04.127 --> 50:05.420
Go ahead and laugh.

688
50:06.254 --> 50:07.547
It's pretty funny.

689
50:16.973 --> 50:18.307
I missed you.

690
50:21.227 --> 50:22.311
You just kept…

691
50:24.021 --> 50:25.231
driving me crazy.

692
50:27.859 --> 50:29.318
I kept…

693
50:31.070 --> 50:32.071
and kept…

694
50:35.658 --> 50:36.784
Just kept…

695
50:40.705 --> 50:41.581
Kept…

696
51:01.684 --> 51:02.977
I missed you.

697
51:05.855 --> 51:07.106
You just kept…

698
51:50.691 --> 51:52.235
Good morning!

699
51:52.360 --> 51:53.361
Morning.

700
51:53.861 --> 51:54.904
MANAGER EOM HO-SIK

701
51:55.029 --> 51:57.114
-Good morning. -Hey.

702
51:58.491 --> 51:59.951
All right…

703
52:02.703 --> 52:03.538
Can we talk?

704
52:15.091 --> 52:16.968
About the incident in the lobby yesterday,

705
52:17.885 --> 52:19.345
I took care of it myself.

706
52:21.722 --> 52:23.891
If HR Manager Jeong glares at you,

707
52:24.016 --> 52:25.560
just ignore him and move on.

708
52:26.477 --> 52:27.562
Wait, what?

709
52:28.396 --> 52:30.481
Did you plead with him for me?

710
52:31.440 --> 52:33.651
And about those posts on the company intranet,

711
52:34.402 --> 52:36.529
they agreed to delete them right away.

712
52:36.654 --> 52:38.781
Best not to look. Stay off it for now.

713
52:40.032 --> 52:42.410
Don't tell me you talked to Manager Shin from DX.

714
52:42.535 --> 52:44.412
Plus, under current company rules,

715
52:44.537 --> 52:46.163
they can't garnish your wages.

716
52:47.290 --> 52:50.209
So don't worry too much about that.

717
52:50.334 --> 52:52.587
Wow, even Finance Manager Yeom?

718
52:54.839 --> 52:56.007
Are you okay?

719
52:56.132 --> 52:58.092
Need anything else?

720
52:58.217 --> 52:59.844
I want the Paris posting.

721
53:02.638 --> 53:05.016
I know my chances are ruined because of this incident.

722
53:06.142 --> 53:09.437
But if you beg General Manager Kang, who knows?

723
53:09.562 --> 53:11.188
Since you're already begging,

724
53:11.314 --> 53:13.274
push a little harder for me.

725
53:13.399 --> 53:14.817
Tell them I really want to go.

726
53:14.942 --> 53:17.069
I'll swat you all the way to Paris!

727
53:20.197 --> 53:21.657
I'm just joking.

728
53:21.782 --> 53:23.117
Hey, do you know

729
53:23.242 --> 53:25.328
what I went through because of you yesterday?

730
53:25.453 --> 53:27.330
I love you. Thank you.

731
53:28.122 --> 53:29.832
Without you, I'd be dragged to HR

732
53:29.957 --> 53:31.334
and sent to the Cheonan factory.

733
53:31.459 --> 53:34.754
I'm nothing without my suit. That was close.

734
53:34.879 --> 53:36.964
What do you mean, "That was close"?

735
53:37.089 --> 53:39.675
Hey, just get lost, will you?

736
53:40.468 --> 53:42.637
Why do I even bother talking to you?

737
53:42.762 --> 53:43.763
Gosh.

738
53:43.888 --> 53:45.848
Speaking of which,

739
53:47.391 --> 53:49.518
you're approving my six-day leave starting tomorrow, right?

740
53:49.644 --> 53:51.812
I asked days ago. Why no approval yet?

741
53:51.938 --> 53:54.523
I already bought my plane tickets. Come on, please hurry.

742
53:54.649 --> 53:55.775
Hey!

743
53:56.525 --> 53:58.319
Are you some travel vlogger?

744
53:58.444 --> 54:00.696
What kind of bullshit are you spouting?

745
54:02.239 --> 54:03.407
That guy…

746
54:04.742 --> 54:06.118
LOVE EAT

747
54:07.495 --> 54:09.246
Where did Pudgy go?

748
54:10.873 --> 54:12.291
Did she get taken?

749
54:12.416 --> 54:13.960
Bambi was hospitalized.

750
54:14.669 --> 54:16.253
She has the herpes virus.

751
54:16.379 --> 54:17.588
It's common for cats.

752
54:17.713 --> 54:19.507
Anyway, she's at the vet.

753
54:25.179 --> 54:26.055
Is it bad?

754
54:26.722 --> 54:27.723
It was at first.

755
54:29.475 --> 54:31.560
But she's fine now. She's eating well.

756
54:32.353 --> 54:34.146
Get her spayed while she's there.

757
54:36.899 --> 54:39.527
Is that really all you have to say to me?

758
54:39.652 --> 54:41.195
I'll be off for six days.

759
54:43.280 --> 54:45.199
Don't be late on the seasoning mix report.

760
54:45.324 --> 54:46.242
I'll check with Sang-hun.

761
54:49.453 --> 54:51.372
I'll help you get that Paris posting.

762
54:56.293 --> 54:57.128
What?

763
54:57.253 --> 55:01.173
I looked into who's testing the waters for the expat position.

764
55:01.298 --> 55:03.551
Your experience and qualifications are far superior.

765
55:03.676 --> 55:04.552
So?

766
55:04.677 --> 55:07.596
I'll make sure you're fully prepared for the interview.

767
55:08.514 --> 55:11.017
The person who went to Germany was my mentor…

768
55:12.101 --> 55:13.060
Why not?

769
55:13.769 --> 55:15.771
You wanted to go to Paris.

770
55:15.896 --> 55:18.190
Ms. Ko got in by acing her interview.

771
55:18.899 --> 55:19.984
Ko Yun-jae?

772
55:20.818 --> 55:22.737
Her husband is Director Im's wife's nephew.

773
55:23.404 --> 55:24.321
Sorry?

774
55:26.699 --> 55:29.285
Just figuring that out, my naive little junior?

775
55:30.494 --> 55:31.620
Jeez.

776
55:34.206 --> 55:36.917
I never even dreamed of getting the Paris position anyway.

777
55:39.086 --> 55:39.962
I just want

778
55:41.172 --> 55:42.965
the launch next year to be successful

779
55:43.632 --> 55:45.760
so I get a bonus… Hey, why the tears?

780
55:45.885 --> 55:47.803
I really wanted you to go.

781
55:49.263 --> 55:50.097
Why are you--

782
55:50.222 --> 55:51.265
I really…

783
55:52.641 --> 55:54.935
I really wanted to help you go.

784
55:56.645 --> 55:57.605
Hey, don't cry…

785
55:58.647 --> 55:59.607
Come on.

786
56:05.529 --> 56:06.655
Everyone's staring.

787
56:08.074 --> 56:10.159
Let's go over there.

788
56:16.332 --> 56:17.708
Are you looking for something?

789
56:18.334 --> 56:21.212
I need a gift for my boyfriend.

790
56:24.882 --> 56:27.510
Something long-lasting that won't wilt.

791
56:27.635 --> 56:30.888
Long-lasting? A dwarf umbrella tree.

792
56:31.013 --> 56:33.224
It symbolizes luck and prosperity, so it makes a great gift.

793
56:33.349 --> 56:34.225
DWARF UMBRELLA TREE

794
56:34.350 --> 56:37.311
And the green color is calming, so it's good for stress, too.

795
56:37.436 --> 56:40.523
It's nice and shiny, right?

796
56:40.648 --> 56:41.857
Will it last forever?

797
56:41.982 --> 56:44.819
Of course. It grows well in the shade, too.

798
56:44.944 --> 56:47.571
With good care, it'll last a long time.

799
56:47.696 --> 56:48.697
I'll take it.

800
56:48.823 --> 56:50.241
Wow, that was fast.

801
56:52.326 --> 56:55.371
To celebrate our opening, customers who spend over 80,000 won

802
56:55.496 --> 56:57.289
get a free gift.

803
57:00.668 --> 57:01.794
Thank you.

804
57:01.919 --> 57:03.838
Depending on the ball's color,

805
57:03.963 --> 57:07.466
you win a chrysanthemum, plant food, or a saucer.

806
57:09.218 --> 57:10.886
Do I just press this button?

807
57:11.011 --> 57:12.680
Yes, just press the button.

808
57:24.233 --> 57:25.734
Damn it.

809
57:30.156 --> 57:31.574
Are you crazy?

810
57:41.250 --> 57:42.084
What's this?

811
57:43.627 --> 57:44.587
A voice recorder.

812
57:46.797 --> 57:49.008
I'll give you some plant food.

813
58:05.482 --> 58:06.442
Ma'am!

814
58:09.278 --> 58:11.655
I just spoke with the detective in charge of Ms. Choi.

815
58:11.780 --> 58:16.035
Ms. Choi stated that Ms. Lee helped fund the fraud for two years.

816
58:16.702 --> 58:20.456
You said you recorded your last meeting with Ms. Choi.

817
58:20.581 --> 58:22.541
Can you send me that file?

818
58:22.666 --> 58:23.918
Yes, I'll send it now.

819
58:43.729 --> 58:44.730
Oh, right.

820
58:45.522 --> 58:46.649
The laptop's broken.

821
58:47.524 --> 58:48.359
Damn it…

822
58:53.280 --> 58:56.116
MIDORI

823
59:36.865 --> 59:38.993
Do you know what you just did?

824
59:46.417 --> 59:49.420
Oh, come on.

825
59:51.714 --> 59:53.424
You don't want to direct, do you?

826
59:54.258 --> 59:55.426
You're scared, aren't you?

827
59:56.427 --> 59:57.511
I WAS SO IMPRESSED

828
59:57.678 --> 59:59.221
INDIE FILM'S NEW HOPE A FAN AS OF TODAY

829
59:59.388 --> 01:00:02.308
LEE MI-DO IS THE BEST

830
01:00:02.474 --> 01:00:04.476
I knew it. You're scared.

831
01:00:05.269 --> 01:00:06.103
No, I'm not.

832
01:00:06.228 --> 01:00:07.271
THE LINES DELIVER THE STORY

833
01:00:07.396 --> 01:00:08.397
That's not it.

834
01:00:09.857 --> 01:00:10.983
Yes, you are.

835
01:00:11.900 --> 01:00:12.776
You want to run away.

836
01:00:12.901 --> 01:00:13.819
WHAT IS A MOVIE?

837
01:00:13.944 --> 01:00:15.696
You're scared and terrified.

838
01:00:16.613 --> 01:00:18.240
I LIKED THE ENDING WHEN THEY PART I LOOK FORWARD TO YOUR NEXT PROJECT

839
01:00:18.490 --> 01:00:20.034
But you feel bad for your boyfriend,

840
01:00:20.701 --> 01:00:22.286
so you're too ashamed to do it.

841
01:00:23.787 --> 01:00:24.621
Am I wrong?

842
01:00:26.290 --> 01:00:27.291
You're wrong.

843
01:00:34.590 --> 01:00:36.216
Want me to help you escape?

844
01:00:38.677 --> 01:00:41.722
You were desperate enough to go beg Song Hae-na,

845
01:00:43.599 --> 01:00:45.684
but I got in the way and ruined it.

846
01:00:47.394 --> 01:00:51.774
You can say you had the talent but just got unlucky.

847
01:00:56.320 --> 01:00:58.572
You got tangled up with some crazy guy,

848
01:00:59.656 --> 01:01:01.408
and got completely screwed over.

849
01:01:05.162 --> 01:01:08.332
Burying a rookie director before they even start

850
01:01:08.999 --> 01:01:11.085
is incredibly easy for me.

851
01:01:13.379 --> 01:01:15.756
Why would you go that far for me?

852
01:01:16.924 --> 01:01:18.675
What do you want from me?

853
01:01:20.511 --> 01:01:21.720
One thing is for sure.

854
01:01:23.180 --> 01:01:24.681
It's not because of the settlement.

855
01:02:32.249 --> 01:02:37.129
DWARF UMBRELLA TREE

856
01:02:37.796 --> 01:02:39.631
You said nothing happened.

857
01:02:39.756 --> 01:02:41.216
That I had nothing to worry about.

858
01:02:41.341 --> 01:02:43.218
I'll just disappear from your life.

859
01:02:43.343 --> 01:02:45.721
I said I'll get out of your life!

860
01:02:45.846 --> 01:02:47.723
What is your problem?

861
01:02:47.848 --> 01:02:49.600
I'm terrible, aren't I?

862
01:02:49.725 --> 01:02:51.059
You must be disappointed.

863
01:02:51.643 --> 01:02:53.729
Ms. Lee and I aren't like that.

864
01:02:53.854 --> 01:02:55.105
Not buying it?

865
01:02:55.230 --> 01:02:57.483
I know everything I say will be an excuse.

866
01:02:57.608 --> 01:03:01.153
Just how miserable do you want to make me?

867
01:03:02.488 --> 01:03:03.322
Mi-do.

868
01:03:03.447 --> 01:03:05.782
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

869
01:03:06.450 --> 01:03:08.410
Subtitle Translation by Cayle Kim
